# CAP mobile app configuration (Expo).
#
# Copy to `.env` (or set these in your shell/CI) to point the app at a real
# backend. Values here are PUBLIC transport config — never put secrets, tokens,
# or PHI in an `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variable; Expo inlines these into the JS bundle.
#
# Leave unset to keep the safe prototype defaults: mock submission and
# UI-only local document handling (nothing is persisted or sent anywhere).
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_SUBMISSION_MODE=mock   # or `api` to POST /intakes
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_UPLOAD_MODE=local      # or `presigned` for two-step upload
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_API_BASE_URL=          # e.g. https://cap-api.example.com
#
# The current mobile build (`packages/mobile/.env`, gitignored) is wired to the
# live deployed Lambda (`cap-api` via API Gateway). The endpoint is public (no
# auth header) and matches the web backend contract verified in
# `planning/handoffs.md`:
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_SUBMISSION_MODE=api
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_UPLOAD_MODE=presigned
# EXPO_PUBLIC_CAP_API_BASE_URL=https://ah0jz85mlj.execute-api.us-east-2.amazonaws.com
#
# Verified against that endpoint (2026-09-05): POST /intakes with a UUIDv4
# Idempotency-Key + URL-encoded EveryAction body returns 201 with a
# CAP-XXXX-XXXX referenceId (idempotent replays return 200 with the same id),
# POST /intakes/:id/upload-url with a JSON {fileName, contentType, size}
# body returns 200 with a real S3 presigned URL, and the byte PUT to that URL
# returns 200 with an ETag — the object lands in the documents bucket. The
# Lambda execution role now has the scoped s3:PutObject policy, so the mobile
# two-step upload (and the web's presigned-S3 adapter) works end-to-end against
# the live endpoint.
